x.q('runtime_hook_and_default_law',6,17,31,'runtime_policy','GTL declares attachment/stable refs/opaque config, HoG reaches, implementation realizes, ABG admits. ABG governs regimes/fallback/proof/closure/observability, not worker internal strategy. Ship broad defaults as ordinary config plus executable hooks; users may copy/edit/reference. Unresolved refs,malformed config,illegal bundles fail closed. Supervised probabilistic dispatch is automated capability, not human review. Optional root supervision selected by admitted system GTL may observe/recover run-wide but cannot wrap repeated start as imperative control and stays distinct from per-edge dispatch/grammar. Composition defaults/templates/fallback/standards/optimization require visible config/published GTL, not code constants,null,prompt/parser,cwd or replay file discovery.')
